Subject: [PATCH 7/7] smb/server: document symbolic link tests and storage

Document the native and xattr-backed representations, client-side path
resolution, mode differences, backup requirements and implementation
limits. Include complete manual mount tests, additional protocol cases
and the KUnit configuration. Runtime code is unchanged by this patch.

Example:

  1. Read fs/smb/server/tests/symlink.rst and create its dedicated share.
  2. Run the POSIX and non-POSIX mount loops in that document.
  3. Remount in both modes to read links created by the other mode.
  4. Boot the KUnit-enabled kernel and check ksmbd-reparse reports
     pass:3 fail:0 skip:0 total:3.

Both mounts must retain relative, directory and dangling link targets.
The document lists validation steps; results from an actual run belong
in the test record, not in the generic test instructions.

Documentation and test instructions generated with OpenAI Codex
assistance.
